invariant: INV-13
file: handshake.c
catches: unit
reason: a ClientHello or client Finished whose send fails keeps the
  handshake's default alert, decode_error, which says the peer sent a
  malformed message, where ch_write names internal_error for the same
  failure. bin/unit fails the first hello's send and requires
  internal_error from ch_alert_sent.

--- old
    int rc = io_send_all(&t->cfg, t->tx, n);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        h->alert = ALERT_INTERNAL_ERROR;
    }
--- new
    int rc = io_send_all(&t->cfg, t->tx, n);
